truth records:

"The source of truth for the project lives in truth records. Every statement in a truth record is a fact that must exist in the project."

"The commander keeps their statements in a txt file with a '.truth' extension. this is a truth record. A topic title lives on the first line with a colon. Statements are placed internally inside quotes, with a line space apart. These are now the source of truth for the project."

"Truth records are stored inside a records/truth directory. They are named using their topic. Each topic should contain truth about a single thing or concept only."

"When the project needs updating or changing, the human changes or adds to their truth statements, not the code."

"Truth records can be replicated or backed up with deterministic tests within the project."

"A truth record gets an agent, or rather an instance of an agent, that ensures the record is truthful when the project is mutated. This agent understands the difference in a file, concept or principle truth record."

"Truth records are locked during any build phase to prevent any agent from mutating them"
